THE WEDGE AS A SCALE PROBLEM: for a core C plus one element w,
   sigma>13  <=>  w > 13*min(C)     and     rho<13  <=>  w < 13*max(C).
So the wedge is a BOUNDED INTERVAL of w per core -- finite, one free parameter.

